The mapping refactor preserves the valid Orbit paths, and the tests meaningfully check copying and aliasing. I found a teacher-target contract mismatch: the new docs promise rejection of every optional-field mismatch, but the preserved implementation silently drops later fields when the first chunk lacks them.

The no-cache mypy run passes for 48 files; the 25 new teacher tests also pass. The full pytest fallback stops with 12 collection errors because PyTorch needs a writable temporary directory, so I cannot independently confirm the recorded 924-pass result here.
